Feature:

Background: This executes once per feature file
	Given these properties
		|portal.release|true|
		|portal.upstream|true|
		|custom.properties|default.layout.template.id=1_column${line.separator}company.default.time.zone=America/Los_Angeles|
		|testray.main.component.name|Calendar|
	And these variables
		|portal.release|true|
		|portal.upstream|true|
		|custom.properties|default.layout.template.id=1_column${line.separator}company.default.time.zone=America/Los_Angeles|
		|testray.main.component.name|Calendar|
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
		|portletName|Calendar|
Setup: This executes before each scenario 
	Given TestCase set Up Portal Instance
	When User first Login PG
	And Page add
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
	Then Portlet add PG
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
		|portletName|Calendar|
Teardown: This executes after each scenario 
	Given PortalInstances tear Down CP
		|testPortalInstance|TestPropsUtil#get('test.portal.instance')|
Scenario: Add Calendar To Current Site Calendars
Priority: 4
	Given TestCase get Site Name
##########################################################
The Poshi return element is not supported in the readable syntax. Please update this test.
##########################################################
		|siteName|${siteName}|
	When Calendar add
		|calendarName|Site Calendar Name|
		|calendarType|Current Site Calendars|
		|site|${siteName}|
	And Navigator goto Page
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
	Then Calendar view
		|calendarName|Site Calendar Name|
		|calendarType|Current Site Calendars|
		|site|${siteName}|
Scenario: Add Calendar To My Calendars
Priority: 4
	Given Calendar add
		|calendarName|My Calendar Name|
		|calendarType|My Calendars|
		|user|Test Test|
	When Navigator goto Page
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
	Then Calendar view
		|calendarName|My Calendar Name|
		|calendarType|My Calendars|
		|user|Test Test|
Scenario: Add User Calendar To Other Calendars
Priority: 4
	Given ProductMenu goto Control Panel Users
		|portlet|Users and Organizations|
	When User add CP
		|userEmailAddress|userea@liferay.com|
		|userFirstName|userfn|
		|userLastName|userln|
		|userScreenName|usersn|
	And Navigator goto Page
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
	And Calendar add
		|calendarName|userfn userln|
		|calendarType|Other Calendars|
	And Navigator goto Page
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
	And Calendar view
		|calendarName|userfn userln|
		|calendarType|Other Calendars|
	Then Calendar view Other Calendar Menulist
		|calendarName|userfn userln|
		|color|668CD9|
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
Scenario: View User Can Add Site Calendars With Calendar Permissions
Priority: 3
##########################################################
The Poshi description element is not supported in the readable syntax. Please update this test.
##########################################################
	When ProductMenu goto Control Panel Users
		|portlet|Roles|
	And RoleNavigator goto Role Type
		|roleType|Site|
	And Role add
		|roleTitle|Calendar Site Role Name|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Users
		|portlet|Roles|
	And Role define Permission CP
		|permissionDefinitionKey|SITE_ADMIN_APPLICATIONS_CALENDAR_MANAGE_EVENTS_CHECKBOX|
		|permissionDefinitionValue|Manage Events|
		|roleTitle|Calendar Site Role Name|
		|roleType|Site|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Users
		|portlet|Roles|
	And Role define Permission CP
		|permissionDefinitionKey|SITE_ADMIN_PAGES_SITE_PAGES_RESOURCE_PERMISSIONS_PAGE_UPDATE_CHECKBOX|
		|permissionDefinitionValue|Update|
		|roleTitle|Authenticated|
		|roleUser|User|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Users
		|portlet|Users and Organizations|
	And User add CP
		|userEmailAddress|usersn@liferay.com|
		|userFirstName|userfn|
		|userLastName|userln|
		|userScreenName|usersn|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Users
		|portlet|Users and Organizations|
	And User edit Password CP
		|userEmailAddress|usersn@liferay.com|
		|userScreenName|usersn|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Sites
		|portlet|Sites|
	And Site add Blank CP
		|siteName|Site A|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Users
		|portlet|Users and Organizations|
	And User edit User Site CP
		|siteName|Site A|
		|userScreenName|usersn|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Sites
		|portlet|Sites|
	And Site add Blank CP
		|siteName|Site B|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Users
		|portlet|Users and Organizations|
	And User edit User Site CP
		|siteName|Site B|
		|userScreenName|usersn|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Sites
		|portlet|Sites|
	And Site add Blank CP
		|siteName|Site C|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Users
		|portlet|Users and Organizations|
	And User edit User Site CP
		|siteName|Site C|
		|userScreenName|usersn|
	And ProductMenu goto Site
		|site|Site A|
	And ProductMenu goto Sites Members
		|portlet|Site Memberships|
	And Site assign Site Role CP
		|resourceName|userfn userln|
		|roleTitle|Calendar Site Role Name|
	And Navigator goto Page
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
	And ProductMenu goto Site
		|site|Site C|
	And ProductMenu goto Sites Members
		|portlet|Site Memberships|
	And Site assign Site Role CP
		|resourceName|userfn userln|
		|roleTitle|Calendar Site Role Name|
	And Navigator goto Page
		|pageName|Calendar Page|
	And User logout And Login PG
		|userLoginEmailAddress|usersn@liferay.com|
		|userScreenName|usersn|
	And UserBar goto Dashboard
	And Portlet add PG
		|portletName|Calendar|
	And User logout And Login PG
		|userLoginEmailAddress|usersn@liferay.com|
		|userScreenName|usersn|
	And UserBar goto Dashboard
	And Calendar search Other Calendars
		|searchValue|site|
	And Calendar view Other Calendars Search Result
		|calendarName|Site A|
	And Calendar view Other Calendars Search Result
		|calendarName|Site B|
	And Calendar view Other Calendars Search Result
		|calendarName|Site C|
	And CalendarNavigator goto Add Event
	And CalendarEvent view Available Calendars
		|availableCalendarList|userfn userln,Site A,Site C|
	Then CalendarEvent view Unavailable Calendars Not Present
		|unavailableCalendarList|Site B,Liferay|

